      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَجِيرٌ</span></b>  (tropical:)  A man's <i>friend,</i> or <i>true</i> or <i>sincere
friend:</i> pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُجَرَآءُ</span>: (S, A, K:) from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَجَرَتِ النَّاقَةُ</span>;
because each of two friends yearns towards the
other. (A.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And hence, (assumed tropical:)  <i>A sword.</i> (Ham
p. 265.)

